findings.recommendation:
Pick one of two fixes; (a) is preferred because it does not leak the unused `pubkey_base58` field over the wire and matches the Solana on-disk convention the server already uses. (a) Webapp side: derive the 64-byte secret from the parsed identity and post `JSON.stringify(parsed.secret)` as `keypair_json`. Concretely:
  const parsed = readIdentity();
  if (!parsed) { ...error... }
  const wire = JSON.stringify(parsed.secret);
  ... body: JSON.stringify({ keypair_json: wire }) ...
Update the existing unit test `send_to_cli_calls_endpoint_and_displays_ticket` to assert `JSON.parse(body.keypair_json).length === 64` and that every entry is a number, instead of `parsedKp.pubkey_base58 === '...'`. (b) Server side: change `bootstrap_redeem_handler` to also accept the object form `{secret: Vec<u8>, pubkey_base58: String}` and prefer it. Either fix unblocks the round-trip; without one of them the CLI will never successfully redeem a ticket issued from the webapp.
